<title>FRANCE: Usinor firms on CAC index entry hopes.</title>
<headline>Usinor firms on CAC index entry hopes.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in steel company Usinor Sacilor rose sharply on Wednesday amid speculation the stock could enter the CAC-40 index on January 13, brokers said.</p>
<p>&quot;Usinor is the obvious candidate,&quot; to take the place of insurer Union des Assurances de Paris (UAP), which is temporarily leaving the index on December 6, while a planned merger with Axa is being considered.</p>
<p>Usinor traded up 3.47 percent to 83.60 francs at 1035 GMT, on volume of 469,190 shares.</p>
<p>The market expects the UAP-Axa merger to go ahead, which would leave a place for a new CAC constituent.  </p>
<p>Insurance company AGF is another CAC candidate but the index is already heavily weighted with financial stocks, one broker said.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +33 1 4221 5452 pnt</p>
